    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="1066" n="932" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    J. C. S. Files</note>
                <head>No. 611<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d611-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C. C. S. 884/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-08">8 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Information for the Russians Concerning the Japanese
                        War</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The United States Chiefs of Staff have considered the proposals of the
                        British Chiefs of Staff in C. C. S.
                            884<anchor n="2" xml:id="d611-f2"/> concerning the information which
                        should be given to the Russians on intelligence, dispositions, and plans in
                        the war against Japan.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The United States Chiefs of Staff consider this matter is not an
                        appropriate one for combined agreement. However, they will not, without
                        prior agreement of the appropriate British authorities, pass to the Russians
                        any information on dispositions or operational plans of Allied forces in
                        areas of British strategic responsibility or any information that has been
                        obtained from a British source.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d611-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d611-f1-content">
                <p>Considered by the Combined Chiefs of Staff at their 196th Meeting, July 19. See
                        <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_113">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 113</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_115"
                    >115</ref>.</p>
            </note>
